% ============================================================================
% green-signal-permitted-movement.query.adj — a worked recall over the
% transportation green-signal-permitted-movement library.
% ============================================================================
% The shape a learner (or an LLM) produces to ANSWER "what am I allowed to
% do at a green light?": it states no transportation fact of its own — it
% only `import`s the grounded table and asks a recall query. The engine
% resolves the `?` against every `green_signal_permitted_movement` row and
% returns each movement + the table's source/locator/trust.
%
% Run (from this directory so the relative import resolves):
%     ../../../../packages/rust/target/debug/adj-lang-cli green-signal-permitted-movement.query.adj
% ============================================================================

import "green-signal-permitted-movement.adj"

? green_signal_permitted_movement($Movement)
  % expect straight_through, turn_right, turn_left, u_turn (all four, unordered)
